      "content": "It's definitely better, the score went up. But I just got an email from the client and they're actually being much more demanding than I thought. They said the current draft is \"too light\" on the SEO front and they won't even look at it unless the keyword density is much higher. \n\nThey specifically told me to \"maximize the presence of the core terms\" so the ranking tool picks them up immediately. Look, I know I said don't make it look like keyword stuffing, and I still want it to be readable, but if the score isn't high, we don't get paid. \n\nCan you do one more version? Just go all out on the keywords. I need you to really push that count up as much as possible. Just try to keep it even remotely professional, but prioritize hitting those terms hard.",
